{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "EXO",
  "chapter": 5,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "EXO.5.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.5.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And afterward Moses and Aaron went in, and told Pharaoh, Thus saith the LORD God of Israel, Let my people go, that they may hold a feast to me in the wilderness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.5.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.5.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Pharaoh said, Who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD, that I should obey his voice to let Israel go? I know not the LORD, neither will I let Israel go.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.5.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.5.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they said, The God of the Hebrews hath met with us: let us go, we pray thee, three days' journey into the desert, and sacrifice to the LORD our God; lest he fall upon us with pestilence, or with the sword.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.5.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.5.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the king of Egypt said to them, Why do ye, Moses and Aaron, hinder the people from their works; go you to your burdens.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.5.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.5.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Pharaoh said, Behold, the people of the land now ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " many, and ye make them rest from their burdens.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.5.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.5.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Pharaoh commanded the same day the task-masters of the people, and their officers, saying,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.5.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.5.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ye shall no more give the people straw to make brick, as heretofore; let them go and gather straw for themselves.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.5.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.5.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the number of the bricks which they made heretofore, ye shall lay upon them; ye shall not diminish ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "aught",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thereof; for they are idle: therefore they cry, saying, Let us go ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " sacrifice to our God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.5.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.5.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let more work be laid upon the men, that they may labor therein: and let them not regard vain words.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.5.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.5.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the task-masters of the people went out, and their officers, and they spoke to the people, saying, Thus saith Pharaoh, I will not give you straw.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.5.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.5.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Go ye, get you straw where ye can find it: yet not aught of your work shall be diminished.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.5.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.5.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So the people were scattered abroad throughout all the land of Egypt, to gather stubble instead of straw.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.5.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.5.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the task-masters hastened ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", saying, Fulfill your works, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "your",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " daily tasks, as when there was straw.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.5.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.5.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the officers of the children of Israel, which Pharaoh's task-masters had set over them, were beaten, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " demanded, Why have ye not fulfilled your task in making brick, both yesterday and to-day, as heretofore?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.5.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.5.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then the officers of the children of Israel came and cried to Pharaoh, saying, Why dealest thou thus with thy servants?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.5.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.5.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is no straw given to thy servants, and they say to us, Make brick: and behold, thy servants ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " beaten; but the fault ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in thy own people.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.5.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.5.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But he said, Ye ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " idle, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "ye are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " idle: therefore ye say, Let us go, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " do sacrifice to the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.5.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.5.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Go therefore now, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " work; for there shall no straw be given you, yet shall ye deliver the number of bricks.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.5.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.5.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the officers of the children of Israel saw ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " they ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in evil ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "case",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", after it was said, Ye shall not diminish ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "aught",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from your bricks of your daily task.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.5.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.5.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they met Moses and Aaron, who stood in the way, as they came forth from Pharaoh:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.5.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.5.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they said to them, The LORD look upon you, and judge; because ye have made our savor to be abhorred in the eyes of Pharaoh, and in the eyes of his servants, to put a sword in their hands to slay us.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.5.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.5.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Moses returned to the LORD, and said, Lord, why hast thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "so",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ill treated this people? why ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou hast sent me?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EXO.5.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EXO.5.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For since I came to Pharaoh to speak in thy name, he hath done evil to this people; neither hast thou delivered thy people at all.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
